or_SMD:R_0402_1005Metric\\\")\"},\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(comp (ref \\\"R49\\\") (value \\\"10\\\") (footprint \\\"Resistor_SMD:R_0402_1005Metric\\\")\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"A 10k series resistor with line and pin capacitance forms a slow RC filter, which can corrupt or limit UART2 communication between NAVC and FCC at normal baud rates.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.4\n    },\n    {\n      \"category\": \"wrong_value\",\n      \"components\": [\"U5\"],\n      \"pins\": [\"U5.7\"],\n      \"nets\": [\"+3.3V\"],\n      \"observed\": \"BMI088 U5 pin 7 (PS, protocol select) is tied to the +3.3V net, although the sensor bus is I2C (SCL/SDA on pins 8/9) with addresses 0x19/0x69 set by SDO pins.\",\n      \"expected\": \"PS should be tied low for I2C operation; tying it high is normally the SPI selection.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(node (ref \\\"U5\\\") (pin \\\"7\\\") (pinfunction \\\"PS\\\") (pintype \\\"input\\\"))  under net (code \\\"1\\\") (name \\\"+3.3V\\\")\"},\n        {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"IMU (accel + gyro) | NAVCPeripherals | Bosch BMI088, I2C addr 0x19 (acc) / 0x69 (gyr)\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"If the protocol-select polarity is as assumed, the IMU would enter SPI mode and fail to respond on the I2C bus. This is low confidence because the reference design may use this strapping on purpose.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.2\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The netlist shows a likely anomaly: the PCA9685 address pin A0 is tied to +3.3V rather than GND, which moves the device off the specified 0x40 address. A smaller candidate is a 10k series resistor on the UART2 line where its partner is 10 ohms.\"\n}",
